Atlanta funded a grocery store =E2=80=94 and more are on the way

Most grocery stores belong to grocery chains =E2=80=94 e.g., Whole Foods, T=
rader Joe=E2=80=99s, Aldi, Kroger, etc. But what if you can=E2=80=99t get t=
hem to open a store in your city?

If you=E2=80=99re Atlanta, you do it yourself. The city put up $8m in fundi=
ng, including grants and loans, to bring Azalea Fresh Market to its downtow=
n =E2=80=94 an area that hasn=E2=80=99t had a supermarket in 20 years =E2=
=80=94 in September, per (https://www.wsj.com/real-estate/commercial/atlant=
a-georgia-public-state-grocery-store-d4e11ad8?mod=3Dhp_lead_pos7&_hsenc=3Dp=
2ANqtz-8T0w2xyXnDtpAcf1S1kdJ9B9iWCwCASQVi2PQQtDB6jY4KyqYYSgnRn0ZxiO9j8s39uM=
IuhyZVBLQolTRsD_wJqNjykQ&_hsmi=3D395297931 ) The Wall Street Journal.

How it works

Savi Provisions, which runs a chain of organic markets, operates the store,=
 purchasing staples wholesale so that it can sell them for less or at parit=
y with major chains. Meanwhile, an upstairs sushi and sandwich counter with=
 beer and wine sold at market prices helps offset the difference.

The city hopes the store will be profitable within three years, and plans t=
o open another six miles away.

Why?

Some neighborhoods are considered =E2=80=9Cfood deserts (https://www.ncbi.n=
lm.nih.gov/books/NBK208016/?_hsenc=3Dp2ANqtz-8T0w2xyXnDtpAcf1S1kdJ9B9iWCwCA=
SQVi2PQQtDB6jY4KyqYYSgnRn0ZxiO9j8s39uMIuhyZVBLQolTRsD_wJqNjykQ&_hsmi=3D3952=
97931 ) =E2=80=9D because access to fresh, affordable food is limited.

Areas that have an abundance of liquor stores and fast-food restaurants, wh=
ere you can buy food but it isn=E2=80=99t healthy, are known as =E2=80=9Cfo=
od swamps (https://uscstoryspace.com/2022-2023/marielag/Fall_Final/?_hsenc=
=3Dp2ANqtz-8T0w2xyXnDtpAcf1S1kdJ9B9iWCwCASQVi2PQQtDB6jY4KyqYYSgnRn0ZxiO9j8s=
39uMIuhyZVBLQolTRsD_wJqNjykQ&_hsmi=3D395297931 ) .=E2=80=9D For obvious rea=
sons, this becomes a health issue.

Atlanta isn=E2=80=99t alone

During his campaign, NYC mayor-elect Zohran Mamdani proposed stores that co=
uld offer lower prices because they=E2=80=99d occupy city-owned buildings, =
rent- and property tax-free.

There=E2=80=99s been a lot of debate as to whether or not that would work, =
and other cities have had mixed results.

- St. Paul, Kansas, funded a supermarket in 2008 and bought it outright aft=
er the couple that ran it retired in 2013. It=E2=80=99s still open. Nearby =
Erie, Kansas, however, bought (https://thehustle.co/the-small-town-that-sav=
