hs-cos-type=3D"rich_text"><h2 style=3D"margin:0; font-size:18px; line-heigh=
t:150%"><span style=3D"font-weight: bold; font-size: 22px;">The billion-dol=
lar blizzard problem</span><br><br></h2>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">If you=E2=80=99ve ever had to dig your car ou=
t from under a snow bank first thing in the morning, you know that the icy =
stuff is not to be messed with.&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">But it can cause bigger problems than making =
you late for work:</p>
<ul style=3D"line-height:150%">
<li aria-level=3D"1">The Federal Highway Administration says the US spends =
<a href=3D"https://media.hubspot.com/e3t/Ctc/UB+113/d2q-Vf04/MX1sj244yR5W1Z=
-p-d2-rnnDVLsY3L5HmGvRN5l4bjq2-ZW0W6N1vHY6lZ3nbV42w2D57hvRrF1FzD8kwNwbW5cwg=
N-3-JlycW8BrWR97MNGqSMq8YlzwKrGsW2cL6766tcYzqW8vWML878p-2MW4FWSKj59H7Y9N49c=
VMS8QD7VW35q6FB3VQLJ2W40fgds1Q7-DNW1WqTvr7JpXDcW2cW7VF2lBKZtW83BslQ8PdxDwW9=
0gF_n2x6kmJW4JB5Z53wtgKFW21gkgF5HFCpHW2jCLnY3M4NqtW20rHcY3nc1l9W4cmcLp34ZDP=
gW5bNmdB1fjxR5N819PtRPWFpKf9cd4bH04" style=3D"color:#192733" data-hs-link-i=
d=3D"0" data-hs-link-id-v2=3D"hykKpivg" target=3D"_blank">$4B+</a> a year j=
ust clearing snow and ice.<br><br></li>
<li aria-level=3D"1">States can <a href=3D"https://media.hubspot.com/e3t/Ct=
c/UB+113/d2q-Vf04/MX1sj244yR5W1Z-p-d2-rnnDVLsY3L5HmGvRN5l4bjK2-ZW0W7lCdLW6l=
Z3lGN7nFHC832ccMV8X-3M4wltvHN84Gdhq8LrsZW5cwyqT7hzp_gN8ln35D_BFFmW73d2T58cP=
YRnW2X7LM130SwXDN2RK75WrTCvWW9crDsw2pjF8LN1yB6hTS-S72W1DjKLk8KNNS_W2t1NbL2v=
fvmcN3Zmv0R2KLyLW8890XZ7mxlrKW11Zq8D2PFkYfW50rJYG3dK2FsW1WrMNQ8bsx1nW7S06RB=
2t3yLNW7YSh6G49STjdW2jfsmT80Ff0mW9hGrXP3z40G-W6yrpvb6c2NJLW7PYt829697MPVlS2=
Jb6sWsNJf6PKKw604" style=3D"color:#192733" data-hs-link-id=3D"0" data-hs-li=
nk-id-v2=3D"PsKINgRf" target=3D"_blank">lose</a> $70m=E2=80=93$700m per day=
 in lost economic activity when facing winter weather shutdowns.</li>
</ul>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">Each winter, cities and states toe a delicate=
, icy line trying to budget just enough for unexpected weather events.&nbsp=
;<br><br></p>
<h2 style=3D"margin:0; font-size:18px; line-height:150%"><span style=3D"fon=
t-weight: bold; font-size: 18px;">A wintry mix&nbsp;</span><br><br></h2>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">Winter cleanup revolves around three things: =
equipment, materials, and staffing.&nbsp;</p>
<ul style=3D"line-height:150%">
<li aria-level=3D"1">Snow plows are among the most important pieces of equi=
pment, and a single one can cost ~$200k. <br><br></li>
<li aria-level=3D"1">States spray millions of gallons of salt brine on road=
s each winter (Utah alone used 2.1m gallons of brine and 202k tons of salt =
in a recent winter, totaling ~$4.3m).</li>
</ul>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">But when storms stack up, budgets explode:</p=
>
<ul style=3D"line-height:150%">
<li aria-level=3D"1">Boston spent $40m in 2014-15 to clear ~110 inches of s=
now =E2=80=94 more than 2x its $18m budget.<br><br></li>
<li aria-level=3D"1">Maryland shelled out $108m after its 2014-15 winter, w=
hich saw 67% more storms.</li>
</ul>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">And the costs don=E2=80=99t stop when the sno=
w melts =E2=80=94 repairs get delayed, potholes multiply, and agencies raid=
 other budgets to stay afloat.<br><br></p>
<h2 style=3D"margin:0; font-size:18px; line-height:150%"><span style=3D"fon=
t-weight: bold; font-size: 18px;">Why cities can=E2=80=99t just =E2=80=9Cpl=
an better=E2=80=9D</span><br><br></h2>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">Winter budgeting is basically a weather guess=
.<br><br>A mild year leaves cities with unused materials and labor; a rough=
 year forces overtime, emergency contractors, and fuel spikes.</p>
<ul style=3D"line-height:150%">
<li aria-level=3D"1">Places built for snow, like Minneapolis (which budgets=
 $13m), bounce back quickly.<br><br></li>
<li aria-level=3D"1">Sunbelt cities often gamble on doing less =E2=80=94 a =
strategy that failed spectacularly for Atlanta in 2014, when a couple inche=
s of snow stranded thousands and cost $2.8m, followed by a $10.7m ice storm=
 two weeks later.</li>
</ul>
<h2 style=3D"margin:0; font-size:18px; line-height:150%"><span style=3D"fon=
t-weight: bold;">A forecasted labor shortage&nbsp;</span><br><br></h2>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">Even well-funded states are short-staffed for=
 snow removal. A 2022 survey found 84% of agencies have higher-than-normal =
plow driver vacancies.<br><br></p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">When the snow hits and the workforce isn=E2=
=80=99t there, the consequences stack up fast.<br><span style=3D"font-size:=
 12px; color: #000000;"> <br></span></p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%"><span style=3D"font-size: 12px; color: #00000=
0;"> </span></p>
